#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185227} :activity/id #uuid "86a338a9-4754-5b43-a262-9a147e4489f2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049317 :topic/id #uuid "ebb1ef31-5cab-5892-affd-92e347cc4f35" :topic/math-academy-id 3817} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185227 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185381 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we wish to find an algebraic expression for $(f \\circ g)(x)$, where\n\n$$\nf(x) = 2x + 3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ng(x) = x - 1\n$$\n\nThe composite function can be calculated by taking the expression for the inner function ${\\color{blue}g(x)}$ and passing it as input to the outer function $f({\\color{blue}x})$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(f∘g)(x) &= f(g(x)) \\\\\n&= 2(g(x)) + 3 \\\\\n&= 2(x - 1) + 3 \\\\\n&= 2x - 2 + 3 \\\\\n&= 2x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we just take the expression for $f$ and replace every occurrence of $x$ with the expression for $g(x)$." :tutorial/id #uuid "7eaa8bd9-f7a4-5d70-b5f6-8cb47bd3a7bd" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9264 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "989b31b4-21ef-50ae-9694-d94b39e208f9" :step/math-academy-id 510974 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185228}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185228 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184340 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183955 :question/id #uuid "150ffc7c-4e70-5f9d-b8e2-8aceacfbd488" :question/math-academy-id "e-14883"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8569b3c6-28a0-5a45-902f-c513e6def877" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049847} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050633}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184731} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184758}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Composite Function"} :step/id #uuid "4a41efa2-c47a-55f7-92f5-0a4a03cee7f0" :step/math-academy-id 510975 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185229}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186185229 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184341 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/